Schema migrations.

    alembic upgrade head          apply everything outstanding
    alembic revision --autogenerate -m "what changed"
    alembic downgrade -1          step back one revision

env.py reads DATABASE_URL through app.config, so there is no connection string
in alembic.ini.

Always read an autogenerated revision before committing it. Autogenerate is
good at columns and constraints and blind to anything that needs data moved.

A database created before these migrations existed will not have the
alembic_version table. If its schema already matches the models, "alembic
stamp head" records the current revision without running anything. If it does
not, and the data is reproducible from the provider, recreating the database
is less work than writing a reconciling revision.
